WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.925
BOD 25-01 is narrower and more concrete.

2
00:00:03.925 --> 00:00:06.650
CISA issued it on December 17, 2024,

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:11.912
for every production cloud tenant
with a finalized SCuBA baseline.

4
00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:17.291
It has six required actions: inventory
the tenants by February 21, 2025;

5
00:00:17.291 --> 00:00:20.722
deploy the SCuBA tools
and report by April 25;

6
00:00:20.722 --> 00:00:25.731
implement the mandatory policies
by June 20; keep up with updates;

7
00:00:25.731 --> 00:00:32.037
baseline every new tenant before its ATO;
and explain deviations with each report.

8
00:00:32.037 --> 00:00:35.426
The mandatory list is a
subset of the baselines.

9
00:00:35.426 --> 00:00:41.728
For Microsoft 365, CISA's Required
Configurations page lists 50 policies;

10
00:00:41.728 --> 00:00:46.100
in Entra ID, that's 20 of the
30 in ScubaGear's baseline.

11
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:52.662
Google Workspace is now in scope too,
with its policies due December 1, 2026.

12
00:00:52.662 --> 00:00:57.650
CISA's guidance limits scope to software
as a service, so Azure subscriptions are

13
00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:02.638
out even when they share the tenant, and
on-premises Active Directory is untouched.

14
00:01:02.638 --> 00:01:06.163
Inventory, deployment and
explanations take days.

15
00:01:06.163 --> 00:01:11.280
Implementing the policies is architecture,
and that's what the directive exists for.
